{
	"_doc": "The colour mood of the picture by time of day (MoodGrade, assets/shaders/mood_grade.gdshader). Keys are blended along the clock (t: 0 = midnight, 0.5 = noon); night holds from the last key to the first. shadow / light: tints multiplied into the dark and the bright parts (1 1 1 = untouched), split: how much of that toning applies, vibrance: extra saturation (dull colours gain most), contrast: gentle S curve, bloom: how much bright things glow, threshold: brightness from which they do, vignette: how far the picture's rim sinks into the shadow tint (0 = none; days keep it faint so the screen stays open, nights let the dark close in). indoors / hex are whole-picture presets for rooms + the mine and the Hexenwald. strength scales everything (0 = off).",
